            <ArticleTitle>An unusual intaocular foreign body.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>348-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An unusual foreign body in a 60-year-old man with ocular siderosis is described. A surgical needle was found in the eye after magnetic resonance imaging was performed for cerebral ischemia. As a general precaution in patients who have undergone any kind of surgery, it might be better to perform a plain x-ray before performing magnetic resonance imaging to identify such foreign bodies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
